## Resolved mutable: m-veg-freeze-streamring-instance-gap

Confirmed real (not hardening-only). client/core/Vegetation.js:601 update() calls streamRing(px,pz) even when cameraStill, every IDLE_STRIDE=16th idle frame. streamRing->loadChunk (Vegetation.js:397/405/416) calls rec.branch.addInstances/rec.leaf.addInstances/sharedImpostor.addImpostors unconditionally. node_modules/@three.ez/instanced-mesh/src/core/feature/Instances.js:92-104 addInstance() only calls setActiveAndVisibilityAt(id,true) and bvh.insert(id) -- no LOD/frustum bucket assignment. node_modules/@three.ez/instanced-mesh/src/core/InstancedMesh2.js:234-248 onBeforeRender: `if (this.autoUpdate && !frustumCullingAlreadyPerformed) performFrustumCulling(camera)` THEN `if (this.count===0) return` -- this.count is only updated inside performFrustumCulling. When frozen (autoUpdate=false, set at Vegetation.js:624 during wantFrozen), performFrustumCulling never runs, so a newly streamed-in instance never enters `this.count`/instanceIndex and stays undrawn for the remainder of the freeze window (until next real camera/rotation movement flips autoUpdate back to true). Classified as already-drifted-bug: fixing now with live browser witness.